  by: agent  # 0f2b
  actor: jgstern_agent  # 0f2b
  clock: 9  # 0f2b
  nonce: 0f2b  # 0f2b
  message: "CLOSURE EVIDENCE 2026-08-24 -- the item's own repro re-run ON THE MERGED TREE\n(dev @dfe3ba8b3e; fix landed PR #510 / c4aaf46ef6), with controls in the same\nrun. Artifacts: ~/hypergumbo_lab_notebook/rilit_closure_08242026/ (run.sh,\nREADME.md, three fresh caches + verdict JSON).\n\nMETHOD. This item's fix is on the PRODUCER; INV-juvul's, which landed first, is\non the SCORER. So re-scoring a PRE-fix cached survey with today's code applies\njuvul's change and not this one -- the ids were already minted. Instrument\nconstant, exactly one hunk differs.\n\n                       PRE                     POST (merged)\n  bellman collisions   10                      0\n  bellman gate         18 (2 spurious)         16 (0 spurious)\n  fixture gate         3                       0\n  caddy modules        158                     158\n  caddy chains         55/76/3 violated        55/76/3 violated\n\nBoth headline figures match what this item filed, to the number. The fixture's\nthree PRE entries were exactly std, std.io, std.net -- verbatim the list in this\nitem's description. Post-fix it emits only the :: spelling.\n\nWHICH HALF THE FIXTURE CONTROLS, stated so it is not overclaimed: the GATE half\nonly. Its collision count is 0 on BOTH arms, because pre-fix it emitted only the\ndotted form for those modules while its imports produced std.io.Write /\nstd.net.UdpSocket -- different folded names, no collision within the run.\nbellman is the positive control for the NODE-IDENTITY half (10 -> 0), which is\nwhat the statement is actually about.\n\nNON-DESTRUCTION at the population level. bellman 862 nodes / 2467 edges\nIDENTICAL both arms; validator 119 cross_field + 1 id_format IDENTICAL, so no\nid was made malformed; distinct entities named 16 on both arms, so the gate's\ndrop from 18 is PURELY duplicate spellings and no entity was lost. caddy is the\ncontrol that matters -- normalize_module_separators folds '/' as well as '::',\nmaking the read-side fold a genuine widening for Go import paths -- and caddy is\nunchanged on every figure.\n\nHONEST LIMIT, unchanged: NO VERDICT FLIPPED. bellman is 3x inconclusive on both\narms, now citing 16 modules instead of 18. What remains is stdlib enumeration\n(WI-lutuh), not normalization.\n\nSTATUS -> satisfied. The statement \"one library entity must have ONE node\nidentity in a run\" now holds on the measured population: 0 rust entities under\nmore than one spelling, down from 10."  # 0f2b
